' =====================================================================
' Design annotations
note left of Restaurant
  <b>Composition</b>: Restaurant creates its Tables and its
  WaitingQueue in its constructor; they live and die with it.
  <b>Encapsulation</b>: every field is private; getTables() and
  getOrders() return read-only lists, so only Restaurant can
  change revenue, the payment queue or the paid satisfactions.
end note

note right of Customer
  <b>Encapsulation</b>: status changes only through
  seatAt() -> placeOrder() -> markServed() -> startEating()
  -> finishEating() -> markPaid(), or leave().
  requireStatus() rejects any step taken out of order.
end note

note bottom of Order
  <b>Encapsulation</b>: billCents is final, so the price
  is locked when the Waiter takes the order.
end note

note top of GameConfig
  <b>Inheritance and polymorphism</b>: GameConfig, Table
  and Customer override Object.toString(). String
  concatenation in ConsoleUI uses GameConfig's
  overridden representation. The custom customer-subtype
  hierarchy is introduced in Stage 2.
end note

note left of TurnController
  Runs every turn in order:
  1 arrivals; 2-3 Waiter, then Chef;
  4 eating and payment (Cashier first);
  5 satisfaction loss and abandonment.
  6 result: runGame() calls isVictory() after turn 18.
  Game rules live in Waiter, Chef, Cashier and
  Restaurant, not in ConsoleUI.
end note

note bottom of ActionResult
  Returned by Waiter.perform(), Chef.prepare() and
  Cashier.processPayment(). An invalid choice returns
  failure(reason); the controller shows it and asks
  again without using up the staff task (brief 3.4).
  Money.format() is used by ConsoleUI, Waiter and Cashier
  to print cents as dollars with two decimals.
end note

